From 46d5c3510c1cc8ba627a65033b45a55a40a50f31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ville=20Kivel=C3=A4?= <vkivela@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:42:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] favicons: rank a page's SVG icon above its raster ones

chatgpt.com declares /favicon.ico sizes="any", a black ICO with 16, 32
and 48 pixel frames, ahead of an SVG that follows prefers-color-scheme.
The tab showed the black ICO under a dark scheme, so the redraw of patch
0025 had nothing to redraw.

FaviconHandler ranks an icon declared for any size, or for none, at 1
before fetching it. It fetched the SVG, drew it once at the largest size
wanted, and scored that one bitmap below 1 against the 16 and 32 pixels
a tab wants. A candidate ranked 1 was still waiting, so it went on to
the ICO, whose exact frames scored 1 and won. Chromium's main branch has
the same favicon_handler.cc as 151, so upstream ranks the same way.

The handler for small icons now sorts a page's SVG candidates before
its raster ones and scores a drawn SVG at 1, since it draws as well at
every size, so it stops there. An SVG that cannot be fetched draws
nothing and the handler goes on to the raster. The largest-icon handlers
for touch icons keep their ranking.

blink::mojom::FaviconURL carries no type from the <link>, so an SVG is
known by its address: a path ending in .svg, or a data: URL of
image/svg+xml, whose path is all that follows the scheme. Nothing a page
can see changes: it is told nothing new, and its links are its own.

svgRanksAboveARasterBesideIt loads a page with qtmulti.ico for any size
ahead of scheme.svg, as chatgpt.com orders them, and fails without this
patch with the ICO's address. svgRanksAboveARasterDeclaredAfterIt
declares the SVG first. Blink reports icons last first, so there the ICO
was fetched first and the SVG never was; it fails the same way, and
covers the sort. rasterShownWhenTheSvgFails names an SVG that does not
exist and passes on both: it guards the fallback.

See villekivela/omaweb#700.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
